v1.5.2: parallel case runs, case debugger, autosave before actions

- OI Cases: compile once per batch, then run cases in parallel
  (up to 2 compilers, up to 4 case workers) with an isolated
  working directory per case; verdicts still arrive in order.
- OI Cases: Debug button runs the selected case through CLion's
  native debugger with the case input redirected to stdin.
- OI Cases: buttons and the time / memory limits now sit on
  separate rows, so they fit a narrow tool window.
- Save the editor before every run, debug, add, remove, clear and
  import, using a write-intent read action (fixes the
  "Access is allowed from write thread only" error on import).
- Judge: line-by-line comparison by position, per-case output
  directories, and compile logs captured to a temp file.
- Import: skip __MACOSX/ and ._* metadata from macOS zips.
- Rebuild the tab strip per file so no stale tabs or scroll
  offsets leak across files, and show a hint for empty case sets.
